{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Common.HookSumGeneral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Common.HookSumGeneral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.armSum_eq_bStat_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.armSum_eq_bStat_conj","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L87-L97","doc":"**Arm sum = `b` of the conjugate** — the general form of the W11\n`Σ_i C(λ_i,2) = b(λ')` observation, proved (via the Fubini `armSum_eq_colSum`)\nfor every `λ` with an explicit column bound `M ≥ λ_0`. This is the reusable\nengine: `Σ_c arm(c) = b(λ')`; the full hook-sum identity\n`Σ_c h(c) = b(λ') + b(λ) + n` then follows from the cell decomposition\n`h = arm + leg + 1` together with `Σ_c leg(c) = Σ_c arm(c over λ') = b(λ)`\n(the leg sum of `λ` is the arm sum of its transpose). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.bStat_conjList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.bStat_conjList","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L77-L85","doc":"`b` of the explicit conjugate equals the column-index sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.conjList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.conjList","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L73-L75","doc":"The conjugate of `λ`, as the list of its first `M` column lengths (`M` any\nbound `≥` the number of columns, i.e. `≥ λ_0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.armSum_eq_colSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.armSum_eq_colSum","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L48-L71","doc":"**The arm-sum double-count** (the Fubini crux): summing the column index `j`\nover the cells of `λ` rows-first equals summing it columns-first,\n`Σ_i Σ_{j<λ_i} j = Σ_j (colLen λ j) · j`, where the column range is bounded by\nthe largest part `M` (any bound `≥ λ_i` for all `i` works; we use `M = λ_0` on a\npartition, but state it for an explicit bound `M` so no sortedness is needed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.armSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.armSum","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L44-L46","doc":"Arm sum `Σ_i C(λ_i, 2) = Σ_i Σ_{j < λ_i} j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.colLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.colLen","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L40-L42","doc":"Length of column `j`: `#{ i : λ_i > j }`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.HookSumGeneral.bStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.HookSumGeneral.bStat","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Common/HookSumGeneral.lean#L37-L38","doc":"`b(λ) = Σ_i i · λ_i` (0-indexed rows). ","signatureChunk":0}]}